<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ShokkweaveEggBlackMarket.xml    ShokkweaveEconomy · WEBWORK_EGG_BLACKMARKET_BUILD_1
  ============================================================================

  §1d/§5 ruling 5 of design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_egg_blackmarket_2026-09-24.md.

  1) Tradeability: RM_OllathrixEgg is Sellable in the free tier (sitting §4a:
     no trader ever STOCKS it there, only nests do). The campaign layer opens
     it to All so `RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_EggMarket` can stock it at all
     (`TraderCanSell()` is false for Sellable — MEASURED in
     ShokkweaveTraderStrip.xml against the same TradeabilityUtility.cs this
     session's sibling item shares).

     🔴 DEPENDENCY, RECORDED HONESTLY: `RM_OllathrixEgg` is
     `WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1`'s own build (in flight concurrently this
     session, not yet landed as of this file). This design's own §4 items
     table places an authoring constraint on that item: the egg must carry an
     EXPLICIT `<tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>` element, not rely on the
     engine's own All default, "or the campaign patch... is a Replace and must
     have a node to match" (the sole-source strip's own lesson: "A patch that
     matches nothing logs nothing" — CLAUDE.md). `PatchOperationConditional`
     below covers BOTH shapes regardless of which one actually ships: Replace
     if the element exists, Add if it doesn't. Until the egg item lands this
     patch's xpath matches nothing and silently no-ops — expected, not a
     defect; re-verify (validate_patch.py, given the defs root and a live def
     dump, and confirm the resulting element reads `All`) once
     `WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1` closes.

     Leak check (§5 ruling 5, "leak-checked at build against every live
     TraderKindDef") — 🔴 CORRECTING the design doc's own §1d claim, found
     wrong while actually running this check: it asserts the egg "belongs to
     no stocked category route." MEASURED 2026-09-26, RimSage against the
     installed 1.6 source: `RM_OllathrixEgg` carries `<thingCategories>
     ResourcesRaw</thingCategories>` (WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1's own file),
     and `StockGenerator_Category categoryDef=ResourcesRaw` is used by FIVE
     live vanilla/DLC TraderKindDefs — `TraderKinds_Base_Outlander.xml`,
     `TraderKinds_Base_Neolithic.xml`, `TraderKinds_Orbital_Misc.xml`
     (Core), `TraderKinds_Base_Empire.xml`, `TraderKinds_Caravan_Empire.xml`
     (Royalty) — none excluding it. `StockGenerator_Category.GenerateThings`
     filters candidates on `tradeability.TraderCanSell()`, which is false for
     Sellable and TRUE for All (same TradeabilityUtility.cs fact the
     sole-source strip measured) — so flipping to `All` alone WOULD let any
     of those five ordinary, extremely common traders randomly roll the
     black-market egg into their stock. The trade-TAG half of the design's
     claim is still correct (`RM_Contraband`: MEASURED, `grep -rn
     "RM_Contraband" src/` across the whole repo returns zero hits outside
     this design's own docs — no `StockGenerator_Tag` anywhere names it).

     FIX (the belt-and-braces this repo already uses for the reverse case —
     ShokkweaveTraderStrip.xml strips Hyperweave's ExoticMisc trade tag the
     same way): campaign-side, strip `ResourcesRaw` off the egg's
     `thingCategories` below. `StockGenerator_SingleDef.HandlesThingDef` is a
     bare defName match with no category dependency, so
     `RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_EggMarket`'s own stocking is untouched; the five
     category-route traders above can no longer see the egg at all. The free
     mod (`mandrake.rm.webwork`) never loads this patch (`MayRequire`), so a
     player without the campaign layer keeps the sitting's own
     `ResourcesRaw`-categorized, nests-only, Sellable-only egg untouched.

  2) The Cartel caravan kind is APPENDED to `RUT_Jawa_HuttCartel`'s own
     `caravanTraderKinds` — Inherit="False" already stands on that def's
     pawnGroupMakers/xenotypeSet for OTHER reasons, but `caravanTraderKinds`
     itself has no such opt-out on this def (see
     UtinniPatches/Defs/FactionDefs/JawaHuttCartel.xml, which already appends
     `RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_Captives` the same way), so this Add appends
     alongside it rather than replacing the list.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.webwork">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_OllathrixEgg"]/tradeability</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_OllathrixEgg"]/tradeability</xpath>
      <value>
        <tradeability>All</tradeability>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_OllathrixEgg"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <tradeability>All</tradeability>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

  <!-- The leak fix: pull RM_OllathrixEgg out of the ResourcesRaw category
       route (see the header note above) once it goes tradeability All.
       Campaign-only, guarded on the same mod. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.webwork">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_OllathrixEgg"]/thingCategories/li[text()="ResourcesRaw"]</xpath>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.webwork">
    <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="RUT_Jawa_HuttCartel"]/caravanTraderKinds</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RUT_Caravan_HuttCartel_EggMarket</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
